  "term": "emotional stability",
  "definition": "Emotional stability is a Big Five personality trait describing how strong and changeable a person’s emotional reactions are when facing stress, setbacks, or negative feelings. Higher emotional stability means steadier emotions and greater resilience, which can help limit worsening anxiety.",
